		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4135&amp;p=31609#p31609"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br><br>Has anyone used the OpenGD77 calibration feature to calibrate a baofeng 1801?  <br>My 1801 is off frequeny (low) by about 700 Hz on 438.1 MHz.<br>I tried using the calibrate feature to recalibrate the radio with no success. <br>The instructions give no clue about how to use this feature.<br>Has anyone used it recalibrate a 1801?  <br>I would be very grateful for any guidance.<br><br>BTW, the 1701 is a great radio.  Too bad its out of production.  I have an 1801 but i prefer the 1701.<br>I especially like the feataure of being able to select talk groups and time slots from a group off TGs for a channel.<br>I wish that they "world standard" Anytone 878 had that feature!!<br><br>Thanks for any help,<br>Dave W4EIP<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2677">W4EIP</a> — Sat Jun 08, 2024 1:39 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
